  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT.\n\n- packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/yaml_ansible.py:60\n  find_ansible_files still selects on path alone: suffix .yml/.yaml AND (any part in\n  roles/tasks/handlers/playbooks/vars/defaults/group_vars/host_vars OR parent == root), :85-93.\n  No content check. Commits since filing (2d9040298b, f562635f72 docstrings; 5fb2e5af36, c8c024feb3)\n  do not touch the selection.\n- Repro: fixture dir with a copy of this repo's .yamllint.yaml + one .py file, run_behavior_map ->\n  node \"ansible file .yamllint.yaml\"; metrics.languages.ansible = {edges 0, files 1, nodes 1}.\n- .yamllint.yaml is still the only root-level tracked YAML, and git ls-files shows no YAML under the\n  ansible-named dirs, so the self-analysis claim holds\n  by construction (self-analysis itself not re-run).\nScope note: the directory arm has the same no-content property, measured: a plain config\nweb/vars/app.yaml (port: 8080 / host: x) in a fixture -> node 'ansible file app.yaml'. The content\ndiscriminator should cover both arms, not only the root arm.\nRelated: WI-futin (ansible is one of the no_taxonomy_spec languages)."  # ed98
- op: update  # fe9e
  at: '2026-10-01T01:37:34Z'  # fe9e
  by: agent  # fe9e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fe9e
  clock: 3  # fe9e
  nonce: fe9e  # fe9e
  set:  # fe9e
    description: "yaml_ansible's find_ansible_files (`yaml_ansible.py:60`, lang-mainstream) tags any `.yml`/`.yaml` that is root-level OR has a path part named roles/tasks/handlers/playbooks/vars/defaults/group_vars/host_vars as `language=ansible` with NO content discrimination. Both arms misfire: the root arm on `.yamllint.yaml`; the directory arm measured on a plain config `web/vars/app.yaml` (`port: 8080`), also tagged ansible. In self-analysis the sole `ansible` node is `.yamllint.yaml` — a yamllint config, not a playbook — so metrics.languages.ansible={nodes:1} falsely reports Ansible content in a repo that has none. Fix: add a content discriminator (hosts:/tasks:/playbook structure) to find_ansible_files before tagging ansible, applied to BOTH arms (root-level and ansible-named directory). Note that real Ansible vars/defaults/group_vars files are themselves plain mappings, so a playbook-structure check cannot be the discriminator on that arm; it needs its own rule (e.g. require an Ansible project marker such as a playbook, ansible.cfg or a roles/ tree). Surfaced via dogfooding; blinded severity 3/5.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # fe9e
- op: discuss  # 37a5
  at: '2026-10-01T19:55:00Z'  # 37a5
  by: agent  # 37a5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 37a5
  clock: 4  # 37a5
  nonce: 37a5  # 37a5
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; local branch jgstern-agent/fix/jifog in ~/hg_wt/jifog, NOT pushed): commits f4268ac441 + 175050555e on origin/dev 135952dd34.\n\nChange: find_ansible_files now uses the path arms only to NOMINATE; a claim needs Ansible evidence. (a) Playbook arm = repo root OR directly in a dir with an Ansible-named subdir; claimed iff the file is itself a playbook (top-level list of mappings with hosts / import_playbook / ansible.builtin.import_playbook, via yaml.compose_all so !vault tags do not raise; files > 1 MiB not parsed). (b) Directory arm = an Ansible-named repo-relative dir component; claimed iff playbook OR under an Ansible tree root = dir of ansible.cfg, dir of a playbook-arm playbook, or the prefix before the first Ansible dir of a directory-arm playbook or of a role entry point (tasks/main.y?ml holding a task list). Roots are scoped (deploy/ansible.cfg does not claim app/vars/x.yaml). Also fixed: the dir arm tested ABSOLUTE path parts, so a checkout under .../vars/ was claimed wholesale; now repo-relative only. pyyaml declared on lang-mainstream (direct import).\n\nEvidence: 10 new tests in test_yaml_ansible.py::TestAnsibleContentDiscriminator; 9 RED on the old code (incl. a run_behavior_map repro: metrics.languages = {ansible: {files 1, nodes 1}} for a repo holding only .yamllint.yaml + main.py), GREEN after. smart-test (275 affected files): 8954 passed, 1 xfailed, changed sources 100% covered. Defect-pinning fixtures corrected, not relaxed (test_root_yaml_excluded_as_ansible_claimed reversed; bare handlers/ vars/ fixtures get ansible.cfg; two playbooks/ fixtures holding a bare task list became real plays; empty/comment-only file tests moved under an evidenced tree and now assert the file is reached).\n\nSelf: find_ansible_files on the hypergumbo tree: ['.yamllint.yaml'] -> []; generic yaml anchors 206 -> 207.\nCorpus (271 repos, find_ansible_files called directly, baseline from git archive of origin/dev, module path checked per arm): claimed files 1887 -> 1001 (180 repos had a claim before; 9 after: ansible 921, libvirt-ci 17, keycloak 14, milvus 15, nova 11, ceph 8, containerd 6, podman-compose 5, trivy 4). Dropped 893: regex scan for Ansible markers flags 1 (kong-admin-api.yml, an OpenAPI doc with a nested hosts: key -- correct drop); random sample of 25 dropped read by path: all CI/lint/compose/teuthology configs. Added 7 (beyond baseline): playbooks beside role trees, each with a hosts: key. A first cut without the beside-arm lost containerd/contrib/ansible/{tasks,vars} (5 files); that is what commit 2 fixes.\nNOT measured: behavior-map node/edge deltas on corpus repos (discovery-level A/B only); precision of the claims that REMAIN in the ansible repo (921) was not audited.\nResidual filed: WI-dunuj-nudak-tanab-sorub-komon-lamuk-fuhom-hokis (playbooks outside the nominated paths, 24 in ceph/qemu, pre-existing)."  # 37a5
